@@ -3,3 +3,13 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` is exported from `src/index.ts` and resolves a
+JSON Pointer string as defined by [RFC 6901](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901.html).
+For example, `resolvePointer({ items: ['first'] }, '/items/0')` returns `'first'`.
+An empty pointer returns the document itself. Member names use `~0` for `~` and
+`~1` for `/`. Malformed pointers and references to missing values throw errors,
+including the array token `-`. Pass a plain pointer string, not a URI fragment
+such as `#/items/0`; percent escapes are treated literally.
+
+Run tests with `npm test` (Node.js 22.18 or newer, with native TypeScript support).
